This is a template for a script. You will need to make modifications as needed. Put it in the tool event page. All it does is go through every event on the map, if the event's name is NPC, turn on its self switch A. Then on the event's A page, you set up the event to do whatever you want it to do.
Code:
$gameMap.events().forEach(event => {
if (event.event().name == "NPC"  && !event._erased && $gameSelfSwitches.value([$gameMap._mapId,event._eventId,'A'])== false)
{$gameSelfSwitches.setValue([$gameMap.mapId(), event._eventId, 'A'], true)}
});
If you want a glow effect on an event use something like MPP Maplight or Hakuen Studio Char Manager. If you want speech bubbles over an event use Aerosys Gab Windows.

Maybe I'm just missing something here?
What I tried:
Create an item in the database and insert the script under the notes (where Moghunter also entered his own notes such as abs-mode, etc.). It doesn't work when I use it.
But when I create a separate event and run it via script:
(function() {
$gameMap.events().forEach(event => {
if (
event.event().name == "NPC" &&
!event._erased &&
$gameSelfSwitches.value([$gameMap._mapId, event._eventId, 'A']) == false
) {
$gameSelfSwitches.setValue([$gameMap.mapId(), event._eventId, 'A'], true);
}
});
})();
Then it works, but regardless of whether I have the item in the slot (the tools are key items in the plugin that have a tool ID in the notes in the database as well as the addition abs-mode) or not or if the Item-key of the script is being pressed (in my case the A-key). ^^'
